{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tibbe/linewright/pulls/1155","id":5275463107,"node_id":"PR_kwDOU_pihc8AAAABOnEtww","html_url":"https://github.com/tibbe/linewright/pull/1155","diff_url":"https://github.com/tibbe/linewright/pull/1155.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/tibbe/linewright/pull/1155.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tibbe/linewright/issues/1155","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tibbe/linewright/pulls/1155/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tibbe/linewright/pulls/1155/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tibbe/linewright/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tibbe/linewright/issues/1155/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tibbe/linewright/statuses/105fad64486a87d86d9d76242beb6e4aff6dd4e0","number":1155,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Capture a stage's run as a case","user":{"login":"tibbe","id":17277,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3Mjc3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17277?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tibbe","html_url":"https://github.com/tibbe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tibbe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tibbe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tibbe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tibbe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tibbe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tibbe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tibbe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tibbe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tibbe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Summary\n\nSpec only. Part of #1151 (the first of #1150's steps): capturing a triage, design or implement run as a case, so that its stage can be run on the same input again. Whole-pipeline capture and replay leave the spec.\n\n```diff\n docs/specs/\n-├── replay.md        # capture a spec change or issue, replay the whole pipeline\n+├── benchmarks.md    # cases: what one run was given, captured from its run\n ├── product.md       # principle \"Tuned against real work\", Areas row\n ├── operation.md     # `capture ID NAME`; a case's items and commits aren't redacted\n ├── design_system.md # the run page offers to capture the run\n └── architecture.md\n GLOSSARY.md          # + Case\n```\n\nA case, as the stage was given it when Linewright decided to start the run:\n\n```text\ncases/<name>/\n  stage, item, start, run ID\n  items        the item, its parent, its spec change, its open filed spec gaps,\n               as GitHub's API gave them, comments before the start only\n  repository   bare git repo: the branch heads at the start and their history, nothing else\n  criteria     what a good result is (optional)\n```\n\n- Input is recorded at each run's start, so only runs from then on can be captured.\n- Kept in GitHub's and git's own terms, not Linewright's prompts or types, so that changes to Linewright leave cases usable.\n- Like Warp Factories' benchmark tasks: pinned commits, plain-text criteria, a pointer to the source run.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `scripts/check markdown model-tables model-quotes model-coverage`: ok.\n- Reviewed with `spec-review` (consistency and writing), with the findings folded in.\n- No UI change.\n\n## Merge Danger\n\n**Door:** two-way\n\nSpec only. The code still has the old `lw capture` and `lw replay` until #1151 is built, and `docs/tuning-briefs.md` still describes them.\n\n**Blast Radius:** spec\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-11-12T10:11:07Z","updated_at":"2026-11-12T10:13:21Z","closed_at":"2026-11-12T10:13:19Z","merged_at":"2026-11-12T10:13:19Z","merge_commit_sha":"c4a839801e4222c8550326de9